  "narrative": "No assessments are due. The registered comparisons add focused follow-up to the accepted dataset-specific architecture without conditioning on the current exposure or outcome. First, I registered direct mean differences that test co-occurrence among the strongest lowering markers: feature_037 within feature_063=1 and feature_003=1, feature_063 within feature_037=1 and feature_003=1, and feature_003 within feature_037=1 and feature_063=1. These are not interaction contrasts; they ask whether a marker that lowers the composite dependency score in one population retains a threshold-level lowering contrast when a second lowering marker is already present. Second, I refined feature_003 localization using high feature_036 with nonpositive feature_018 after removing feature_010, feature_037, and feature_063, and separately high feature_036 after excluding feature_037 and feature_063 while allowing feature_010. These address whether the feature_036-amplified feature_003 contrast is merely clean-cell structure or survives different conditioning choices. Third, I mapped feature_063 in feature_010-positive but feature_037-negative individuals and in feature_010-negative but feature_037-positive individuals, clarifying whether feature_063 lowering is attenuated by feature_010 and whether it persists when feature_037 is present. Fourth, I tested the positive raw feature_010 contrast within feature_037=1 after excluding feature_003 and feature_063, and in a clean population with high feature_036 and nonpositive feature_018, to test whether the feature_010 axis remains identifiable in lower-marker and marker-intersection contexts. Finally, I registered a broad nominal feature_059 level_001 versus level_003 screen after excluding the two dominant binary axes. All estimates are signed to the claimed direction, judged against the 0.15-unit threshold, and interpreted only as unadjusted associations in the supplied dataset with a composite dependency endpoint; exclusion-based conditioning can induce selection-like patterns, and no causal, single-gene, or external generalizability claim is made. No validation is requested because the voluntary validation budget is exhausted.",
  "research_notes": "Validation budget exhausted. Current dataset-specific model remains: feature_037 is the largest robust lowering association; feature_010 is context dependent, positive in low/moderate feature_038 contexts and reversing strongly negative when feature_038 and feature_018 are both nonnegative; feature_003 lowering localizes to high feature_036; feature_063 lowering is context dependent, strongest in clean low-feature_010/low-feature_037 or low-feature_018/high-feature_038 regions. New registrations test co-occurrence among feature_037, feature_003, and feature_063; broader feature_003 high-feature_036 localizations with nonpositive feature_018 or with feature_063/feature_037 excluded but feature_010 allowed; direct feature_063 contrasts in feature_010-positive/feature_037-negative and feature_010-negative/feature_037-positive contexts; direct feature_010 contrasts within feature_037=1 and in clean high-feature_036/nonpositive-feature_018 cells; and a feature_059 nominal screen. Analysis priority: co-occurrence contrasts with adequate cells, then feature_003 and feature_063 localizations, then feature_010 refinements, then nominal screen. All conclusions remain dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable claims."
